From 301990a8e9eef369391f2ab2901df0596c071d9f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 15:51:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Scope renewal: take the renewing identity from the
 whole process ancestry

renew-scope read the session and the Kanban task from the CLI process's own
environment, which its parent chooses. An agent, including a run of the stopped
card, could name the owning chat's session and drop its task markers to renew
as that chat.

The session and task now come from the start-time environment of every
ancestor: a task marker anywhere counts, the card's own run is refused first,
and an ancestry that does not name exactly the claimed session has no identity.
An unreadable ancestry is refused.

Also pass the task id to the TUI spend notice so it prints the real
renew-scope command.
---
